    "username": "AnthropicAI",
    "text": "New Anthropic Fellows research: Returning to the neuron basis for interpretability\n\nUnderstanding what’s happening inside an AI model helps to make it safer. One obvious place to look is its neurons, or the simple units it’s built from. Early interpretability work did just that, but over the past couple years, researchers largely moved on from that idea, for three reasons: a single neuron often fires on several unrelated inputs, the way a concept is represented can change between two layers of n",
